   "he": "יַיִן וְנִמְצָא חוֹמֶץ – שְׁנֵיהֶן יְכוֹלִין לַחֲזוֹר בָּהֶן. לֵימָא מַתְנִיתִין רַבִּי הִיא וְלָא רַבָּנַן? דְּתַנְיָא:",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If the seller sold «wine and it is found» to be «vinegar, both» the seller and the buyer «can renege on» the sale. The Gemara suggests: «Shall we say» that «the mishna is» in accordance with the opinion of «Rabbi» Yehuda HaNasi «and not» in accordance with the opinion of «the Rabbis? As it is taught» in a baraita:"
